 "drivingQuestion": "What is the scriptural source for exiting backward, facing the sanctuary?",
 "outcome": "inconclusive",
 "outcomeNote": "The derivation is completed in the next unit (מקיש יציאתו לביאתו)",
 "continuesQuestionOf": null,
 "segments": [
  {
   "id": "yoma.53a.21",
   "daf": "53a",
   "sentenceId": 20,
   "he": "יָצָא וּבָא לוֹ דֶּרֶךְ כְּנִיסָתוֹ. מְנָא הָנֵי מִילֵּי? אָמַר רַבִּי שְׁמוּאֵל בַּר נַחְמָנִי, אָמַר רַבִּי יוֹנָתָן, אָמַר קְרָא: ״וַיָּבֹא שְׁלֹמֹה לַבָּמָה אֲשֶׁר בְּגִבְעוֹן יְרוּשָׁלִַם״, וְכִי מָה עִנְיַן גִּבְעוֹן אֵצֶל יְרוּשָׁלַיִם?",
   "en": "§ The mishna teaches that the High Priest «exits and comes» out «the way» that «he entered,» i.e., he does not turn around, but walks backward with his face toward the Ark. The Gemara asks: «From where are these matters» derived; what is the source in the Torah for this halakha? «Rabbi Shmuel bar Naḥmani said» that «Rabbi Yonatan said» that «the verse states: “And Solomon came to the high place that was at Gibeon, Jerusalem”» (II Chronicles 1:13). «Now, what does Gibeon have to do with Jerusalem?» Either he came to Gibeon or to Jerusalem; these are two different places."
  }
 ],
